# Contributing to {{ project_name }}
## Conventional commits
- `feat[(scope)]: description` → MINOR, `fix[(scope)]:` → PATCH, `feat!:` / `BREAKING CHANGE:` → MAJOR
- Other types `docs|style|refactor|perf|test|build|ci|chore|revert` hidden unless `!`
- Scope is noun, description imperative present, lowercase, no period, ≤72 chars
- Enforced by `commitlint` + `husky` (`npx commitlint --from=origin/main --to=HEAD`)
## Changelog
`CHANGELOG.md` `## [Unreleased]` gated by `scripts/changelog-gate.py` in `changelog-check.yml` (a PR run reads the `Landing:` declaration from the PR body; the `main` run is the durable one); `release.yml` runs `semantic-release`, whose `scripts/release-changelog.mjs` plugin promotes the curated ledger into the versioned section and re-opens an empty `## [Unreleased]`. Do not hand-edit versioned sections. Commit a sync as a hidden type (e.g. `chore: sync changelog unreleased section`) so it mints no ledger entry. Hidden types only appear when `!`/`BREAKING CHANGE`.
## Release
Cut a release from `main` with the release workflow; five phases run in order, and each exits `0` before the next starts.
1. Check — working tree clean, on `main`, conventional commits.
2. Verify — `pnpm run verify` passes; it is the same gate CI runs.
3. Preview — a dry run prints the next version and its release notes.
4. Dispatch — run the release workflow and wait for it to succeed.
5. Confirm — the tag is reachable from `main` and `CHANGELOG.md` has the versioned section.

The ledger decides the bump. A user-facing feature needs a `feat` title; a breaking entry needs `!` in the title. A `fix` title licenses a patch and cannot publish a `### Features` entry.
## Reporting Issues
Pick the template that matches your intent — see `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/` (blank issues disabled).
- Bugs: paste-complete, prefer text over screenshots.
- Features: state problem + proposal at minimum; alternatives optional.
## Before PR
`pnpm run verify` must pass — one command, one exit code. It runs lint → format → typecheck → test in the order CI gates them (the coverage script when this project gates coverage). See `AGENTS.md` for agent rules.
## Pull Requests
Prefer topic branch → PR → squash merge. Keep one concern per PR; link the issue with `Closes #NN`.
### Description
PR body follows the repo's resolved PR template: `.github/pull_request_template.md` when present, else the gh-router canonical `skills/gh-router/references/pull_request_template.md` (install with `bash skills/gh-router/scripts/install-template.sh --target .`). Follow the resolved template's headings and order.
CI (`changelog-check.yml`, `verify`) must be green before requesting review.
